# Paths that are deliberately credential-shaped.
#
# A secret scanner's tests have to contain realistic, non-allowlisted
# credentials to prove that real ones are not suppressed -- so scanning this
# repository reported its own fixtures at confidence 0.9. Widening the allow
# patterns to cover them would create silent false negatives, which is the one
# failure mode worse than noise.
#
# A per-line secscan:ignore directive covers the working tree, but history keeps
# the version of the line from before the directive existed, and rewriting
# published history to quiet a scanner is a bad trade. This file covers both.

main_test.go
